  "limits": [
    "Evidence belongs exclusively to Hepta 8b0fd11dde9f13ac784b3579ec9930ae4832784d and upstream NDU 2590c0c94c5bf9a9004caeeb7b75edd6faf3eb8b. Later Windows Clang or other changes are not execution-qualified by this campaign.",
    "Authored v1 acyclic scalar u8 recurrence on one Linux x86_64 host. This is not v8 borrowed-view execution, Rust resource parity, C/C++ migration, cross-platform performance, or general compiler refinement evidence.",
    "All 48 episodes retained the original generation. No successful publication, rollback, hot state transfer, heap/loan/stack migration or background replacement was exercised in this formal campaign.",
    "276 timing-driver stdout strings and full child status records are retained. NDU stores structured request/response and transport identity, not the original subprocess stdout/stderr byte stream or independent syscall trace.",
    "The six native NDU decision records are distinct from build/initialization identity probes. Six does not mean the total number of all executable launches during bridge construction and initialization.",
    "Fresh proof receipts are bound to actual source/program bytes but were not rerun by this read-only audit. The encoder, canonical verifier, solver, compiler, linker and host remain trusted; no machine proof of encoder or native refinement follows.",
    "Recorded tool hashes cover Clang, cargo, rustc and the bridge builder. Python/Z3 versions are reported; their historical executable/library bytes and objdump executable bytes are not fully captured by this campaign. The disassembly bytes were instead checked directly against the retained ELF symbol bytes.",
    "Artifact and directory identity closure is observed in 48 runtime cleanup records, including successful one-shot closes of 96 identity pins, zero pending resources and absent paths at close observation. At this later audit 43 of 48 historical directory paths are absent; five exist with different inodes and no files. No permanent path absence, attribution of those replacements, hostile concurrent filesystem-race defense or kernel-level remote attestation is claimed.",
    "Prepared candidate/calibration libraries and selected-artifact copies are intentional retained evidence outside the private runtime cleanup domain; zero pending runtime resources does not mean every evidence file is deleted.",
    "Cold means an empty NDU cargo target with existing offline dependencies and installed tools. It is not a fully cold host. Build child CPU time can exceed wall time and is separately reported.",
    "Direct baseline pays actual required common setup only. Same-information rows additionally charge calibration; single-episode columns are counterfactual unamortized setup charges. Physical study wall time must not be obtained by summing these standalone deployment counterfactuals.",
    "Warm online publication gating explicitly excludes the one-off cold bridge build; final cold net-benefit accounting includes it. Every candidate was rejected before publication in this run.",
    "Empirical min/max batches are not confidence intervals. Two repetitions per profile, a shared nonexclusive host and one frozen workload family do not support statistical significance or general NDU superiority.",
    "No failed attempt is present among this completed campaign's observed samples; audit confirms all records are counted. This does not erase the separately retained earlier development failures or make a universal failure-handling claim."
  ],
